# Linux Server Health-Check Project

## Scenario

A Linux server continuously collects and processes data from external
Internet sources.

If the workload stops functioning, the underlying cause could exist
at several layers.

## Troubleshooting Model

SYSTEM
CPU → Memory → Disk → Processes

NETWORK
Interface → IP → Route → Gateway → Internet

SERVICES
DNS → Ports → Application/API

EVIDENCE
Logs → Packet Capture

uptime
free -h
df -h
ps aux
ip -brief addr
ip route
ping -c 2 1.1.1.1
dig example.com
ss -tulpn
journalctl

scripts/network_health_check.sh

#!/bin/bash

echo "=========================="
echo " NETWORK HEALTH CHECK"
echo "=========================="

echo
echo "=== INTERFACES ==="
ip -brief addr

echo
echo "=== ROUTING TABLE ==="
ip route

echo
echo "=== DEFAULT GATEWAY ==="
ip route | grep default

echo
echo "=== INTERNET CONNECTIVITY ==="
ping -c 2 1.1.1.1

echo
echo "=== DNS ==="
dig google.com

echo
echo "=== LISTENING PORTS ==="
ss -tulpn

